I have created a tool `fetch_page.ts` that fetches the content of a URL and extracts the main text by stripping out `<script>` and `<style>` tags.

### The Tool
I used Bun's native `fetch` API to retrieve the content.

```typescript
// fetch_page.ts
import { Buffer } from 'node:buffer';

const url = "https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/redesigning-source-control";

async function fetchPage() {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(url);
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`Failed to fetch: ${response.statusText}`);
    }
    const html = await response.text();

    // Simple text extraction: remove script and style tags
    const cleanText = html
      .replace(/<script\b[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/script>/gmi, '')
      .replace(/<style\b[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/style>/gmi, '')
      .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ')
      .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
      .trim();

    console.log(cleanText);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error fetching page:", error);
  }
}

fetchPage();
```

### Execution
You can run it using Bun:
```bash
bun fetch_page.ts
```

### Output Preview
The tool successfully extracted the article content, beginning with:
> "Redesigning source control at Anthropic ... As our merges per day grew more than tenfold, source control became our biggest development bottleneck. Here, we share how we migrated to an in-house version control system in five months..."

